The attached image characterizes the physical properties of Nano-11 nanoparticles, a dendrimer-like α-D-glucan vaccine adjuvant. The left panel, a Transmission Electron Microscopy (TEM) image (Fig. 2A in the PDF), shows the spherical, irregular, and cauliflower-like appearance of the nanoparticles, which exist primarily as single units. The right panel, a histogram derived from dynamic light scattering (DLS) (Fig. 2B in the PDF), illustrates the size distribution, indicating a consistent Z-average hydrodynamic diameter for Nano-11 particles ranging from 75 to 80 nm, a key characteristic for efficient uptake by dendritic cells and their biological function.